---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  lang="en"
  title="SDD CLI Documentation | Architecture, OpenSpec, Lifecycle & Commands"
  description="Comprehensive documentation for SDD-CLI: OpenSpec directory anatomy, 7-phase deterministic lifecycle, RFC 2119 specs, CLI commands, and AI agent integration."
>
  <div class="space-y-16">
    <!-- Header intro banner -->
    <header class="pb-8 border-b border-sdd-border">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-sdd-accent/30 bg-sdd-accent/10 text-sdd-accent text-xs font-mono mb-4">
        <span>Spec-Driven Development CLI</span>
        <span class="text-sdd-border">•</span>
        <span>Version 0.5.0</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-mono font-bold text-sdd-text tracking-tight mb-4">
        SDD CLI <span class="text-sdd-accent">Technical Documentation</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-sdd-muted font-sans leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        SDD CLI enforces deterministic, specification-first engineering workflows for autonomous AI coding agents. 
        It replaces speculative "vibe-coding" with explicit human checkpoints, normative RFC 2119 language contracts, and git-native OpenSpec directories.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Section 1: Overview & Philosophy -->
    <section id="overview" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border text-sdd-accent font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">01</span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-mono font-bold text-sdd-text">Overview & Philosophy</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-sdd-muted space-y-4 font-sans text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          As Large Language Models (LLMs) and autonomous programming agents (such as Antigravity, Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, OpenCode, and Codex) evolve, their speed in outputting code exceeds human ability to safely review diffs. Left unbounded, agents make silent architectural assumptions, introduce hallucinated parameters, degrade unit test validity, and accumulate brittle technical debt.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-sdd-text font-mono">Spec-Driven Development (SDD)</strong> introduces a simple yet foundational shift: <strong class="text-sdd-accent font-mono">No AI agent writes code before a human approves the specification.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Core tenets cards -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border">
          <div class="text-sdd-accent font-mono font-bold text-sm mb-1">Explicit Intent</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-sdd-muted leading-normal">
            Problems, goals, and non-goals are pinned before any architectural diagram or code module is designed.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border">
          <div class="text-sdd-accent-alt font-mono font-bold text-sm mb-1">Contractual Truth</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-sdd-muted leading-normal">
            Acceptance criteria are specified with RFC 2119 keywords and Given/When/Then scenarios that double as test suites.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border">
          <div class="text-sdd-warning font-mono font-bold text-sm mb-1">Human Gate Sovereignty</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-sdd-muted leading-normal">
            Transitions between phases require explicit human sign-off. Agents are gate-blocked from advancing prematurely.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 2: Why SDD vs Vibe-Coding -->
    <section id="why-sdd" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border text-sdd-accent font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">02</span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-mono font-bold text-sdd-text">Why SDD vs Vibe-Coding</h2>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sdd-muted font-sans text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        "Vibe-coding" is the antipattern of feeding unstructured, open-ended conversational prompts to an AI and hoping the synthesized implementation matches unstated business constraints. Compare the two paradigms:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs font-mono border border-sdd-border rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
          <thead class="bg-sdd-elevated text-sdd-text uppercase border-b border-sdd-border">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3">Dimension</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-red-400">Vibe-Coding (Unconstrained)</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-sdd-accent">SDD (Spec-Driven Development)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-sdd-border bg-sdd-bg">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-text font-bold">Initial Trigger</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-muted">Vague chat prompt: "add auth and stripe payments"</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-accent-alt">Structured discovery: <code class="text-sdd-text">proposal.md</code> with problem, scope & non-goals</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-text font-bold">Requirement Clarity</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-muted">Implicit assumptions, subjective LLM interpretations</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-accent-alt">Normative RFC 2119 keywords (<code class="text-sdd-accent">MUST</code>, <code class="text-sdd-accent">SHOULD</code>, <code class="text-sdd-accent">MAY</code>)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-text font-bold">Control Points</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-muted">None. Agent modifies 30 files across repository simultaneously</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-accent-alt">4 review gates before any application code is touched</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-text font-bold">Acceptance Testing</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-muted">"Looks right in browser" or synthetic shallow tests</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-accent-alt">Deterministic Given/When/Then criteria validated by <code class="text-sdd-text">sdd verify</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-text font-bold">Historical Audit</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-muted">Lost in ephemeral chat threads and squashed git commits</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-sdd-accent-alt">Permanent audit trail archived in <code class="text-sdd-text">openspec/changes/archive/</code></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3: RFC 2119 & Given/When/Then -->
    <section id="rfc-2119" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border text-sdd-accent font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">03</span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-mono font-bold text-sdd-text">RFC 2119 & Given / When / Then Standards</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4 text-sdd-muted font-sans text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          LLMs excel when prompt ambiguity is reduced to zero. In SDD, all functional specifications in <code class="text-sdd-text">specs.md</code> MUST adhere to internet standards established in <strong class="text-sdd-text">IETF RFC 2119</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 font-mono text-xs">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border">
          <div class="text-sdd-accent font-bold mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-sdd-accent/10 border border-sdd-accent/40">MUST / MUST NOT</span>
            <span class="text-sdd-text text-[11px]">Absolute Requirements</span>
          </div>
          <p class="font-sans text-sdd-muted text-xs leading-relaxed">
            Non-negotiable criteria. If the agent fails to satisfy any MUST statement or executes a MUST NOT condition, the verification gate categorically fails.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-3 p-2.5 rounded bg-sdd-bg border border-sdd-border text-[11px] text-sdd-text">
            "The authentication token <span class="text-sdd-accent font-bold">MUST</span> expire after 15 minutes of inactivity."
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border">
          <div class="text-sdd-accent-alt font-bold mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-sdd-accent-alt/10 border border-sdd-accent-alt/40">SHOULD / MAY</span>
            <span class="text-sdd-text text-[11px]">Recommended & Optional</span>
          </div>
          <p class="font-sans text-sdd-muted text-xs leading-relaxed">
            Valid reasons may exist in particular circumstances to ignore SHOULD items, but the full implications must be understood and documented.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-3 p-2.5 rounded bg-sdd-bg border border-sdd-border text-[11px] text-sdd-text">
            "Responses <span class="text-sdd-accent-alt font-bold">SHOULD</span> include an ETag header for client-side caching."
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Given/When/Then Example -->
      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border space-y-3">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <h4 class="font-mono font-bold text-sm text-sdd-text">Behavioral Acceptance: Given / When / Then</h4>
          <span class="text-[11px] font-mono text-sdd-accent">Gherkin-Style Determinism</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-sdd-muted font-sans">
          Every requirement in <code class="text-sdd-text">specs.md</code> is paired with behavioral test cases formatted as:
        </p>
        <pre class="p-3.5 rounded-lg bg-sdd-bg border border-sdd-border text-xs text-sdd-text overflow-x-auto"><code>#### Scenario 1: Expired session refresh
- **Given** an authenticated user whose JWT expired 3 minutes ago
- **When** a request is made to `/api/v1/user/profile` with a valid refresh cookie
- **Then** the service MUST issue a new pair of tokens with HTTP 200
- **And** the user session activity timestamp MUST update in Redis</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 4: Human Gate System -->
    <section id="human-gates" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border text-sdd-accent font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">04</span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-mono font-bold text-sdd-text">The Human Gate System</h2>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sdd-muted font-sans text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        SDD CLI does not slow down AI agents; it places guardrails exactly where human judgment is vital. 
        Each gate transitions state from <strong class="text-sdd-warning font-mono">Pending (Amber)</strong> to <strong class="text-sdd-accent font-mono">Approved (Green)</strong> only after explicit review:
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between p-4 rounded-lg bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border gap-2">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-sdd-accent/10 border border-sdd-accent/40 text-sdd-accent">Gate 1</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-sdd-text font-bold">Proposal Sign-off</span>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs text-sdd-muted font-sans">Validates problem definition, user impact, non-goals, and business alignment.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between p-4 rounded-lg bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border gap-2">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-sdd-accent/10 border border-sdd-accent/40 text-sdd-accent">Gate 2</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-sdd-text font-bold">Specs Validation</span>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs text-sdd-muted font-sans">Ensures RFC 2119 compliance and complete Given/When/Then acceptance coverage.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between p-4 rounded-lg bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border gap-2">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-sdd-accent/10 border border-sdd-accent/40 text-sdd-accent">Gate 3</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-sdd-text font-bold">Design & Architecture Check</span>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs text-sdd-muted font-sans">Reviews database schema migrations, API contracts, security vectors, and trade-offs.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between p-4 rounded-lg bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border gap-2">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-sdd-accent/10 border border-sdd-accent/40 text-sdd-accent">Gate 4</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-sdd-text font-bold">Atomic Task Breakdown</span>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs text-sdd-muted font-sans">Approves ordered, granular implementation checklist. The agent is locked from coding before this gate passes.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 5: OpenSpec Directory Anatomy -->
    <section id="openspec-anatomy" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border text-sdd-accent font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">05</span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-mono font-bold text-sdd-text">OpenSpec Directory Anatomy</h2>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sdd-muted font-sans text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        SDD repositories follow the standardized <strong class="text-sdd-text font-mono">OpenSpec</strong> filesystem structure under <code class="text-sdd-text">openspec/</code>. 
        This directory is versioned directly in Git alongside your project source code.
      </p>

      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border font-mono text-xs text-sdd-text">
        <div class="text-sdd-accent font-bold mb-3">// Standard OpenSpec Tree Layout</div>
        <pre class="bg-sdd-bg p-4 rounded-lg border border-sdd-border/80 overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed"><code>.
├── AGENTS.md                          <span class="text-sdd-muted"># System prompt instructions & rule boundaries</span>
├── openspec/
│   ├── config.yaml                    <span class="text-sdd-muted"># Project configuration & gate rules</span>
│   ├── specs/                         <span class="text-sdd-muted"># Baseline permanent system specifications</span>
│   │   ├── auth.spec.md
│   │   ├── billing.spec.md
│   │   └── api-gateway.spec.md
│   ├── changes/                       <span class="text-sdd-muted"># Active feature proposals in flight</span>
│   │   └── 2026-09-18-oauth2-flow/
│   │       ├── proposal.md            <span class="text-sdd-muted"># Phase 1: Problem statement & scope</span>
│   │       ├── specs.md               <span class="text-sdd-muted"># Phase 2: RFC 2119 & Given/When/Then</span>
│   │       ├── design.md              <span class="text-sdd-muted"># Phase 3: Technical architecture</span>
│   │       └── tasks.md               <span class="text-sdd-muted"># Phase 4: Atomic step checklist</span>
│   └── changes/archive/               <span class="text-sdd-muted"># Immutable log of completed & merged specs</span>
│       ├── 2026-08-01-initial-db/
│       └── 2026-08-20-rate-limiter/
└── src/                               <span class="text-sdd-muted"># Production application source code</span></code></pre>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2 font-mono text-xs">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-sdd-bg border border-sdd-border">
          <div class="text-sdd-accent-alt font-bold mb-1">openspec/specs/</div>
          <p class="font-sans text-sdd-muted text-xs leading-relaxed">
            The evergreen, living truth of your architecture. When a change archives, relevant modifications merge back into baseline specs here.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-sdd-bg border border-sdd-border">
          <div class="text-sdd-accent font-bold mb-1">openspec/changes/</div>
          <p class="font-sans text-sdd-muted text-xs leading-relaxed">
            Active changes currently going through the 7-phase cycle. Each change contains its own 4-stage document set.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-sdd-bg border border-sdd-border">
          <div class="text-sdd-warning font-bold mb-1">openspec/changes/archive/</div>
          <p class="font-sans text-sdd-muted text-xs leading-relaxed">
            Frozen, read-only audit records of past changes after passing Phase 6 (Verify) and Phase 7 (Archive).
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 6: config.yaml -->
    <section id="openspec-config" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border text-sdd-accent font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">06</span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-mono font-bold text-sdd-text">openspec/config.yaml Specification</h2>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sdd-muted font-sans text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        The <code class="text-sdd-text">config.yaml</code> file controls verification strictness, automated test commands, file path glob patterns, and language enforcement:
      </p>

      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3 text-xs font-mono">
          <span class="text-sdd-text font-bold">openspec/config.yaml</span>
          <span class="text-sdd-accent">YAML Schema v1</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="bg-sdd-bg p-4 rounded-lg border border-sdd-border text-xs text-sdd-text overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed font-mono"><code>version: "1.0"
project:
  name: "ecommerce-api"
  language: "typescript"
  package_manager: "pnpm"

standards:
  rfc2119: true
  acceptance_format: "given_when_then"
  spec_language: "en"             # Specs & code must strictly be English

verification:
  test_command: "pnpm test:run"
  lint_command: "pnpm lint"
  typecheck_command: "pnpm tsc --noEmit"
  strict_rfc_check: true

gates:
  require_proposal_approval: true
  require_spec_approval: true
  require_design_approval: true
  require_task_approval: true</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 7: The 7-Phase Lifecycle Deep Dive -->
    <section id="phase-1-proposal" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border text-sdd-accent font-mono text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">07</span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-mono font-bold text-sdd-text">The 7-Phase Lifecycle Deep Dive</h2>
      </div>

      <!-- Phase 1 -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-sdd-border pb-3">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xl">📄</span>
            <h3 class="font-mono font-bold text-lg text-sdd-text">Phase 1: Proposal (<code class="text-sdd-accent">proposal.md</code>)</h3>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-sdd-accent/10 border border-sdd-accent/40 text-sdd-accent">Gate 1</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm font-sans text-sdd-muted leading-relaxed">
          The purpose of the proposal is to clearly articulate the problem, why existing solutions are insufficient, what success looks like, and what is explicitly OUT of scope.
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-sdd-bg border border-sdd-border text-xs font-mono space-y-2">
          <div class="text-sdd-accent-alt font-bold">Standard proposal.md Sections:</div>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-sdd-muted space-y-1">
            <li><code class="text-sdd-text">## Context & Problem Statement</code> — The exact friction or missing capability.</li>
            <li><code class="text-sdd-text">## Proposed Solution Summary</code> — High-level technical direction.</li>
            <li><code class="text-sdd-text">## Scope & Inclusions</code> — What will be built in this change.</li>
            <li><code class="text-sdd-text">## Non-Goals & Out of Scope</code> — Explicit bounds preventing scope creep.</li>
            <li><code class="text-sdd-text">## Human Sign-off</code> — Checkbox for the authorized engineer.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Phase 2 -->
      <div id="phase-2-specs" class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border space-y-4 scroll-mt-24">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-sdd-border pb-3">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xl">📋</span>
            <h3 class="font-mono font-bold text-lg text-sdd-text">Phase 2: Specs (<code class="text-sdd-accent">specs.md</code>)</h3>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-sdd-accent/10 border border-sdd-accent/40 text-sdd-accent">Gate 2</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm font-sans text-sdd-muted leading-relaxed">
          Transforms intent into mathematically unambiguous requirements. Every item is phrased using RFC 2119 keywords accompanied by comprehensive Given/When/Then scenarios.
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-sdd-bg border border-sdd-border text-xs font-mono space-y-2">
          <div class="text-sdd-accent-alt font-bold">Verification Criteria:</div>
          <p class="font-sans text-sdd-muted text-xs leading-relaxed">
            Must specify exact status codes, error payload schemas, boundary conditions, timeout limits, and idempotency guarantees.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Phase 3 -->
      <div id="phase-3-design" class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-sdd-elevated border border-sdd-border space-y-4 scroll-mt-24">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-sdd-border pb-3">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xl">⚙️</span>
            <h3 class="font-mono font-bold text-lg text-sdd-text">Phase 3: Design (<code class="text-sdd-accent">design.md</code>)</h3>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-sdd-accent/10 border border-sdd-accent/40 text-sdd-accent">Gate 3</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm font-sans text-sdd-muted leading-relaxed">
          The engineering blueprint. Documents technical architecture, data model migrations, external dependencies, sequence flows, security considerations, and rejected alternatives.
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-sdd-bg border border-sdd-border text-xs font-mono space-y-2">
          <div class="text-sdd-accent-alt font-bold">Key Deliverables:</div>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-sdd-muted space-y-1">
            <li>Database schema diffs (DDL, indexing, foreign keys)</li>
            <li>Public API / RPC contracts (OpenAPI, GraphQL or Proto schemas)</li>
